API reference

An OpenAI-compatible gateway. Point any OpenAI SDK at the base URL below and swap the key. Every endpoint on this page, supported or not, is read from the generated contract in this repository.

Quickstart

Create a key under API keys, export it as HIVE_API_KEY, then call the gateway exactly as you would call OpenAI.

BASE URL
https://api-hive.scubed.co/v1
AUTHENTICATION
Authorization: Bearer <your key>
curl
curl https://api-hive.scubed.co/v1/chat/completions \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $HIVE_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "model": "hive-default",
    "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Say hello in one sentence."}]
  }'
Python, official OpenAI SDK
# pip install openai
import os

from openai import OpenAI

client = OpenAI(
    base_url="https://api-hive.scubed.co/v1",
    api_key=os.environ["HIVE_API_KEY"],
)

response = client.chat.completions.create(
    model="hive-default",
    messages=[{"role": "user", "content": "Say hello in one sentence."}],
)
print(response.choices[0].message.content)

hive-default is a routing alias, not a single upstream model. See the model catalog for what each alias resolves to and what it costs.

Machine-readable spec

The OpenAPI document this page is generated from. Point your own tooling at it rather than reading this page.

Served unauthenticated at /api/openapi.yaml on this console's own origin · 97 operations described · support matrix version 0.1.0, generated 2026-03-28

The generation date is printed because it is the honest measure of how current this page is. Nothing here is hand maintained, so if that date is old, the classifications below are that old too.

Where the spec and the support matrix disagree

75 operations are described differently by the two generated files: 75 the matrix classifies but the spec never describes, 0 the two give different support statuses, 0 the spec declares but the matrix never classified. All of them are listed rather than one file being silently preferred, because either side can be the stale one.

