BUILD
Hive Auto

Automatic routing: each request gets a per-request model choice and is billed at actual usage.

Try in chat
Back to catalog
hive-auto
Preview
stable
chat
responses
task-aware
IN / OUT PRICE
Variable / Variable
Variable / Variable credits, per 1m tokens
CACHE READ / WRITE
Variable / Variable
Variable / Variable credits, per 1m tokens
CONTEXT
Not published
The catalog carries no context window for this alias.
PRICING MODE
Variable
Charged from the cost the upstream reports per request.
Pricing

This alias is priced from the actual cost of each generation, so it publishes no per-million rate. The charge is derived per request, not from a table.

DIMENSION	PRICE / 1M	CREDITS / 1M	WHAT IT COVERS
Input	Variable	Variable	Prompt tokens sent to the model.
Output	Variable	Variable	Tokens the model generates.
Cache read	Variable	Variable	Prompt tokens served from an upstream prompt cache.
Cache write	Variable	Variable	Prompt tokens written into an upstream prompt cache.
Providers and uptime

Hive routes each request across the providers configured for this alias. Per-provider figures are held in the control plane but are not served to the console today, so they are shown as absent rather than guessed.

Per-provider pricing
Route-level prices exist in the routing snapshot, which no customer-facing endpoint returns.
Latency and throughput
Per-request timings are recorded, but no per-provider percentile is computed or served.
Uptime
Route health is tracked for failover decisions only and is not exposed as an availability figure.
Benchmarks
Hive publishes no independent benchmark scores for catalog models.
